Dial every offered relay at once, bounded by a context, and start without the slow ones.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, on top of 0002 (upstream PR #26).

Why: PR #26 binds every relay in the offer one after the other, each behind a 12 s
timeout that only stopped waiting: the connect itself took no context, so a relay
that blackholes its handshake held the call for 12 s before any media (once per such
relay) and then kept its socket and goroutines, still handshaking, for as long as
the process ran. Now:

- relay.ConnectRelayMediaContext closes the UDP socket when its context ends, which
  fails the handshake in progress and releases what it had allocated;
- connectOneRelay gives each connect a 12 s context derived from the call's;
- connectAndAllocateAll dials every relay concurrently, starts the fanout once the
  first is up and the others had 2 s, and closes any that connects later.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387, rounds 2b and 4. Measured
against a local UDP blackhole: the context-bound connect returns at the deadline and
its goroutines drain; ConnectRelayMedia without it is still connecting after 5 s.

